1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:07,121
<font color="#000000">Large vision models trained by autoregression
promise a single generalist model for many visual tasks,</font>

2
00:00:07,201 --> 00:00:13,822
<font color="#000000">but today's versions demand billions of parameters
and hundreds of billions of visual tokens to train.</font>

3
00:00:13,902 --> 00:00:18,159
<font color="#000000">This ICML 2024 paper, DeLVM, asks whether we really
need all that.</font>

4
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:21,443
<font color="#000000">The authors show that two simple, classical ideas,</font>

5
00:00:21,523 --> 00:00:24,400
<font color="#000000">data augmentation and knowledge distillation,</font>

6
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:30,181
<font color="#000000">let a compact autoregressive vision model reach
strong performance on a limited dataset,</font>

7
00:00:30,261 --> 00:00:35,700
<font color="#000000">cutting both the parameter footprint and the
training data requirement dramatically.</font>

8
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,670
<font color="#000000">In language modeling,</font>

9
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:43,340
<font color="#000000">autoregressive models like GPT thrive on a
universal token interface.</font>

10
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:47,010
<font color="#000000">Recent work extends this idea to vision,</font>

11
00:00:47,090 --> 00:00:50,680
<font color="#000000">treating images and annotations as visual sentences.</font>

12
00:00:50,760 --> 00:00:54,350
<font color="#000000">But the leading large vision model needs over three
billion parameters and roughly four</font>

13
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:58,020
<font color="#000000">hundred billion visual tokens drawn from more than
a billion images.</font>

14
00:00:58,100 --> 00:01:01,690
<font color="#000000">That scale is expensive and impractical for edge
deployment.</font>

15
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:05,360
<font color="#000000">Worse,</font>

16
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:09,030
<font color="#000000">the visual world is long-tailed: some tasks like
segmentation have abundant data while</font>

17
00:01:09,110 --> 00:01:12,700
<font color="#000000">others like pose estimation are starved,</font>

18
00:01:12,780 --> 00:01:16,370
<font color="#000000">and training on the raw mixture leaves the model
unable to learn the rare tasks at all.</font>

19
00:01:16,750 --> 00:01:23,017
<font color="#000000">Language models are typically trained for a single
epoch over vast corpora to avoid overfitting.</font>

20
00:01:23,097 --> 00:01:27,976
<font color="#000000">Computer vision rarely has that luxury: many tasks
have only tiny datasets,</font>

21
00:01:28,056 --> 00:01:31,546
<font color="#000000">so the language training schedule does not carry over.</font>

22
00:01:31,626 --> 00:01:36,108
<font color="#000000">At the same time, the community keeps scaling model
and dataset size,</font>

23
00:01:36,188 --> 00:01:39,810
<font color="#000000">while classical remedies for scarce and imbalanced data,</font>

24
00:01:39,890 --> 00:01:43,248
<font color="#000000">namely data augmentation and knowledge distillation,</font>

25
00:01:43,328 --> 00:01:47,215
<font color="#000000">have barely been tried in the autoregressive vision
setting.</font>

26
00:01:47,295 --> 00:01:49,000
<font color="#000000">This paper closes that gap.</font>

27
00:01:49,380 --> 00:01:52,938
<font color="#000000">The authors make three main contributions.</font>

28
00:01:53,018 --> 00:01:56,577
<font color="#000000">First, they show that simple data augmentation,
random crop and flip,</font>

29
00:01:56,657 --> 00:02:00,215
<font color="#000000">rebalances long-tailed multi-task data and improves
an autoregressive vision model just</font>

30
00:02:00,295 --> 00:02:03,853
<font color="#000000">as effectively as collecting more real samples.</font>

31
00:02:03,933 --> 00:02:07,492
<font color="#000000">Second,</font>

32
00:02:07,572 --> 00:02:11,130
<font color="#000000">they bring knowledge distillation to autoregressive
large vision models for the first time,</font>

33
00:02:11,210 --> 00:02:14,768
<font color="#000000">using a LLaMA one-billion teacher to lift a compact
three-hundred-million student across</font>

34
00:02:14,848 --> 00:02:18,407
<font color="#000000">single-task and multi-task benchmarks.</font>

35
00:02:18,487 --> 00:02:22,045
<font color="#000000">Third, they build a practical
eighty-million-parameter model that,</font>

36
00:02:22,125 --> 00:02:25,683
<font color="#000000">combining both techniques,</font>

37
00:02:25,763 --> 00:02:29,322
<font color="#000000">surprisingly reaches eighty-three percent top-one
accuracy on ImageNet,</font>

38
00:02:29,402 --> 00:02:32,960
<font color="#000000">suggesting generation and understanding can be
learned together.</font>

39
00:02:33,340 --> 00:02:38,345
<font color="#000000">Experiments cover three core tasks.</font>

40
00:02:38,425 --> 00:02:43,430
<font color="#000000">Image segmentation uses subsets of SA-1B ranging
from one to ten percent;</font>

41
00:02:43,510 --> 00:02:48,515
<font color="#000000">human pose estimation uses the full COCO-Pose
dataset; image deraining uses Rain13K.</font>

42
00:02:48,595 --> 00:02:53,600
<font color="#000000">Validation relies on held-out SA-1B splits together
with MPII and Test2800.</font>

43
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:58,685
<font color="#000000">The distilled models are also benchmarked on Pascal
five-i foreground segmentation using mean intersection-over-union,</font>

44
00:02:58,765 --> 00:03:03,770
<font color="#000000">and the practical eighty-million model is evaluated
on ImageNet classification.</font>

45
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:08,855
<font color="#000000">Throughout,</font>

46
00:03:08,935 --> 00:03:13,940
<font color="#000000">the VQGAN tokenizer is trained on the Laion dataset
and used off the shelf.</font>

47
00:03:14,320 --> 00:03:17,517
<font color="#000000">The results consistently favor the proposed recipe.</font>

48
00:03:17,597 --> 00:03:19,702
<font color="#000000">On the mixed three-task benchmark,</font>

49
00:03:19,782 --> 00:03:26,128
<font color="#000000">balancing the data through augmentation beats both
the raw unbalanced mixture and naive re-sampling,</font>

50
00:03:26,208 --> 00:03:29,020
<font color="#000000">which actually collapses on the scarce tasks.</font>

51
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:33,711
<font color="#000000">Knowledge distillation then improves the compact
student on segmentation,</font>

52
00:03:33,791 --> 00:03:38,595
<font color="#000000">pose estimation, and deraining, in both single-task
and multi-task training.</font>

53
00:03:38,675 --> 00:03:42,129
<font color="#000000">On the Pascal five-i foreground segmentation benchmark,</font>

54
00:03:42,209 --> 00:03:49,262
<font color="#000000">the distilled and fine-tuned three-hundred-million
model clearly surpasses the same model trained from scratch.</font>

55
00:03:49,342 --> 00:03:54,981
<font color="#000000">And scaling data on segmentation from one to ten
percent lowers validation loss by nearly</font>

56
00:03:55,061 --> 00:03:58,323
<font color="#000000">two tenths and perplexity by over twenty-two points,</font>

57
00:03:58,403 --> 00:04:02,050
<font color="#000000">an effect augmentation reproduces with no new data at all.</font>

58
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:04,787
<font color="#000000">Several ablations sharpen the picture.</font>

59
00:04:04,867 --> 00:04:09,276
<font color="#000000">Changing the prompt background color changes the
generated background,</font>

60
00:04:09,356 --> 00:04:15,690
<font color="#000000">and using black-background prompts makes a simple
grayscale-threshold post-processing step reliable.</font>

61
00:04:15,770 --> 00:04:21,590
<font color="#000000">Training without shuffling the task data triggers
catastrophic forgetting: the model becomes</font>

62
00:04:21,670 --> 00:04:24,604
<font color="#000000">proficient only on its most recently seen task,</font>

63
00:04:24,684 --> 00:04:28,581
<font color="#000000">with perplexity on earlier tasks exploding into the
thousands,</font>

64
00:04:28,661 --> 00:04:33,070
<font color="#000000">underscoring that shuffling is essential for
multi-task LVMs. Finally,</font>

65
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:35,571
<font color="#000000">even at just eighty million parameters,</font>

66
00:04:35,651 --> 00:04:40,702
<font color="#000000">knowledge distillation still improves validation
perplexity across segmentation,</font>

67
00:04:40,782 --> 00:04:42,690
<font color="#000000">pose estimation, and deraining.</font>

68
00:04:43,070 --> 00:04:45,260
<font color="#000000">The takeaway is refreshingly simple.</font>

69
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:50,620
<font color="#000000">You do not need a three-billion-parameter model and
hundreds of billions of tokens to</font>

70
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:53,394
<font color="#000000">build a capable autoregressive vision model.</font>

71
00:04:53,474 --> 00:04:54,970
<font color="#000000">Two classical techniques,</font>

72
00:04:55,050 --> 00:05:01,528
<font color="#000000">data augmentation to rebalance long-tailed tasks
and knowledge distillation to compress a large teacher,</font>

73
00:05:01,608 --> 00:05:07,140
<font color="#000000">together let compact models trained on limited data
perform strongly across segmentation,</font>

74
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:09,094
<font color="#000000">pose estimation, and deraining.</font>

75
00:05:09,174 --> 00:05:14,517
<font color="#000000">That an eighty-million-parameter version even
reaches eighty-three percent accuracy on</font>

76
00:05:14,597 --> 00:05:16,598
<font color="#000000">ImageNet points toward efficient,</font>

77
00:05:16,678 --> 00:05:21,390
<font color="#000000">deployable generalist vision models that unify
generation and understanding.</font>
